    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's an interesting way to look at it, but i feel like that ignores the technical side of things. if an artist is so focused on the message that they stop caring about composition, color theory, or actual craft, doesn't that basically mean the art itself is failing? like, can you even call it 'good' art if it's just a political poster in a gallery frame?",
